#question(title: [Proof of Theorem 3])[
  #set text(size: 13pt)
  Write a proof for the following Theorem
  #slide-block(title: [#set text(size: 13pt)
  Theorem 3])[
    Let $display({a_n}_(n = 0)^oo)$ be a
    sequence.
    - IF $display({a_n}_(n = 0)^oo)$ is
      increasing AND unbounded above,
    - THEN $display({a_n}_(n = 0)^oo)$ is
      divergent to $oo$
  ]

  + Write the definitions of “increasing",
    “unbounded above", and “divergent to
    $oo$"
  + Using the definition of what you want to
    prove, write down the structure of the
    formal proof.
  + Do some rough work if necessary.
  + Write a formal proof.
]
